# 2026-09-07: investigated a -0.005 ns setup violation on the vendored HDMI
# PLL clock (pll_hdmi|...|divclk, Slow -40C corner, TNS -0.022 ns) that
# appeared after this session's SDRAM cache widening (rtl/suna8_media_sdram.sv,
# commits 634f776/43db98d). The failing endpoints are in sys/ HDMI video
# logic this session did not touch; core logic's own 24 MHz domain closes
# with 13+ ns of slack in every corner. The immediately preceding accepted
# build (commit f24388b) closed this same corner at +0.038 ns, so the extra
# cache logic's routing/placement pressure measurably tightened it -- a real,
# if small, regression, not a pre-existing condition.
#
# Tried SEED 2 (-0.715 ns, TNS -4.426), SEED 3 (-0.181 ns, TNS -1.102) and
# SEED 4 (-0.028/-0.365 ns, two corners) -- the three additional seeds the
# mister-rbf-build skill allows. None beat the unseeded default's -0.005 ns.
# Deliberately left unseeded (best result of everything tried) rather than
# pinning a worse seed. This is a genuine active timing miss, not proven
# false or inactive, so it is NOT waved through as a reviewed exception --
# see docs/COMPLETION_PLAN.md section 3d for the full record and required
# next step (sys/ hazard review) before this can be accepted as a release
# build.


# 2026-09-12 (R084 build, commit 223019f): the unseeded default missed by -0.024 ns
# (TNS -0.072) on the pll_hdmi divclk (sys/ HDMI video logic; the core's own clocks
# had 7.5+ ns). SEED 5, the first seed tried, closes every corner: setup +0.245,
# hold +0.067, recovery +3.974, removal +0.235, min pulse +1.041, TNS 0. Placement
# only; no RTL, SDC, PLL or sys/ change.
set_global_assignment -name SEED 5
